From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yoon <5332544+yoonda9@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:27:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] win: fs and process fallbacks for pre-Vista

Uses the run-time pointers from the first patch, compiled only when the
legacy-fallbacks macro is set; upstream lines are unchanged and move into
#else branches.

- env_strncmp: CompareStringOrdinal absent -> ordinal compare of UTF-16
  code units upper-cased with RtlUpcaseUnicodeChar (ntdll), the
  invariant table CompareStringOrdinal itself uses.
- fs__realpath: GetFinalPathNameByHandleW absent -> UV_ENOSYS before the
  file is opened (the call sites follow a7493d8a^).
- fs__fchmod: ReOpenFile absent -> UV_ENOSYS.
- fs__symlink: CreateSymbolicLinkW absent -> UV_ENOTSUP (junctions still
  work).
- fs__open (UV_FS_O_FILEMAP) and the fs-event pending-delete check:
  uv__file_standard_info, which calls GetFileInformationByHandleEx when
  it exists and NtQueryInformationFile(FileStandardInformation) when not.
- uv__kill SIGQUIT minidump: skipped when RegGetValueW,
  SHGetKnownFolderPath or SetFileInformationByHandle is missing;
  uv__once_init() first, since uv_kill may run before any loop.
- NeedCurrentDirectoryForExePathW absent -> TRUE unless
  NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath is set.
---
 src/win/fs-event.c |  4 +++
 src/win/fs.c       | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/win/process.c  | 73 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/win/winapi.c   | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++
 src/win/winapi.h   |  7 +++++
 5 files changed, 161 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/win/fs-event.c b/src/win/fs-event.c
